  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-112309",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The fungi culture $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $30%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nFrom the given information, we have the following:\n\n- $a=5$ is the initial number of fungi.\n\n- $r=0.3$ is the growth rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in weeks, since the culture started.\n\nSo, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =5\\cdot (1+0.3)^{t} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (1.3)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the number of weeks it takes for the fungi culture to increase to $100,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =100 \\\\ 5\\cdot (1.3)^{t} & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
